{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"Unlock global AI inference scalability using new global cross-Region inference on Amazon Bedrock with Anthropic’s Claude Sonnet 4.5 | Artificial Intelligence","context":"## Request limit increases for global CRIS with Anthropic’s Claude Sonnet 4.5\n\nWhen using global CRIS inference profiles, you can use global CRIS from over 20 supported source Regions. Because this will be a global limit, requests to view, manage, or increase quotas for global cross-Region inference profiles must be made through the Service Quotas console or AWS Command Line Interface (AWS CLI) in the requested source Region.\n\nComplete the following steps to request a limit increase:\n\n1. Sign in to the Service Quotas console in your AWS account.\n\n[](https://d2908q01vomqb2.cloudfront.net/f1f836cb4ea6efb2a0b1b99f41ad8b103eff4b59/2026/10/23/REVBLOG-1365-1.jpg)\n\nFigure 1: The Service Quotas console\n\n2. In the navigation pane, choose **AWS services**.\n3. From the list of services, find and choose **Amazon Bedrock**.\n4. In the list of quotas for Amazon Bedrock, use the search filter to find the specific global CRIS quotas. For example:\n\n * Global cross-Region model inference tokens per minute for Anthropic Claude Sonnet 4.5 V1.\n5. Select the quota you want to increase.\n6. Choose **Request increase at account level**.\n\n[](https://d2908q01vomqb2.cloudfront.net/f1f836cb4ea6efb2a0b1b99f41ad8b103eff4b59/2026/10/23/REVBLOG-1365-2.jpg)\n\nFigure 2: Requesting a quota increase at the account level\n\n7. Enter your desired new quota value.\n8. Choose **Request** to submit your request.\n\nWhen calculating your required quota increase, remember to take into account for the burndown rate, defined as the rate at which input and output tokens are converted into token quota usage for the throttling system. The following models have a **5x burn down rate for output tokens (1 output token consumes 5 tokens from your quotas):**\n\n* Anthropic Claude Opus 4.\n* Anthropic Claude Sonnet 4.5.\n* Anthropic Claude Sonnet 4.\n* Anthropic Claude 3.7 Sonnet.\n\nFor all other models, the burndown rate\n\n*[truncated — additional content omitted]*","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/unlock-global-ai-inference-scalability-using-new-global-cross-region-inference-on-amazon-bedrock-with-anthropics-claude-sonnet-4-5/"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"Claude Sonnet 5","context":"## Programmatic Access\n\nUse the following model IDs and endpoint URLs to access this model programmatically. For more information about the available APIs and endpoints, see APIs supported and Endpoints supported.\n\n**Important:**\n\nThis model is offered through one or more inference profiles designated as inference profiles with limited model selection. These profiles are expected to offer a narrower selection of models, and new models or model versions might not be released for them. Before you take a dependency on one of these inference profiles, review Inference profiles with limited model selection and plan for model lifecycle events.\n\n| **Endpoint** | **Model ID** | **In-Region endpoint URL** | **Geo inference ID** | **Global inference ID** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `bedrock-runtime` | `anthropic.claude-sonnet-5` | N/A | `us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5` `eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5` `au.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5` `in.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5` | `global.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5` |\n| `bedrock-mantle` | `anthropic.claude-sonnet-5` | `https://bedrock-mantle.{region}.api.aws/anthropic/v1/messages` | N/A | N/A |\n\n*For example, to use Global cross-Region inference from us-east-1 (N. Virginia), use the endpoint URL \"https://bedrock-runtime.us-east-1.amazonaws.com\" with the inference profile ID \"global.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5\".*","url":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-card-anthropic-claude-sonnet-5.html"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"How do I improve Amazon Bedrock performance and response times when I process and retrieve large scale data?","context":"### Use Cross-Region Inference\n\n[Cross-region inference](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/cross-region-inference.html) routes your requests across multiple AWS Regions using inference profiles. You can [choose geographic profiles or global profiles](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/cross-region-inference.html#cross-region-inference-comparison). Cross-region inference reduces throttling when you reach regional capacity limits. Cross-region inference improves availability but can add cross-region latency. All data stays on the AWS network and is encrypted in transit","url":"https://repost.aws/knowledge-center/bedrock-improve-performance-latency"}]}}

